.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-DOMAIN-ADD" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-domain-add - Serve a tunnel route at a hostname under a verified workspace domain (pb domain add)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel domain add <tunnel> <hostname> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Serve one route of a tunnel at a hostname under a verified workspace domain: for example
app.example.com when example.com is added and verified with pb domain add and pb domain verify.
The domain's verification and certificate cover the hostname, so there is no DNS step of its
own. --route picks the route the hostname serves.

.PP
A change returns once the request is accepted, and the tunnel may still be connecting. Pass
--wait to wait (at most --timeout, default 2m, 1s to 10m) until it finishes, or check pb tunnel
status.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--route\fP=""
	route to serve at the hostname

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	maximum time to wait for operation completion

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	wait for the operation to reach a terminal state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb tunnel domain add web app.example.com --route route_xyz
  pb tunnel domain add web app.example.com --route route_xyz --wait
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel-domain(1)\fP
